{"id":5264,"date":"2018-03-07T16:57:32","date_gmt":"2018-03-07T21:57:32","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/?p=5264"},"modified":"2020-03-07T21:31:07","modified_gmt":"2020-03-08T03:31:07","slug":"rotterdam-the-netherlands","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/travel-log\/rotterdam-the-netherlands\/","title":{"rendered":"Rotterdam, the Netherlands"},"content":{"rendered":"<p>Being between Germany and the UK, the Netherlands was a strategic position that both the Allies and the Axis wanted to control during the Second World War. Since the Netherlands had decided to remain neutral like it had been during the First World War, the German military believed that the Netherlands would be an easy target. That was not the case and the battle for Rotterdam lasted several days.<\/p>\n<p>The story goes that during this battle, a German general told Rotterdam to either surrender or the German army will blow up the entire city. The Dutch colonel refused to surrender and stalled for more time. The second time that the German army gave the Dutch the ultimatum, the Dutch colonel was ready to surrender. The messenger had however given the wrong time and the German army flattened the city minutes before news of surrender would have reached the German army. For this reason, the vast majority of the city buildings date from the late 20th century. When deciding how to rebuild, the city opted to breath fresh life into the city with new building designs.<\/p>\n<p>Known for its eclectic architecture, Rotterdam is definitely a unique destination to visit!<\/p>\n<p>A special thank you to <a href=\"https:\/\/freewalkingtourrotterdam.com\/your-guides\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><u>Free Walking Tour<\/u><\/a> for all of the information.<\/p>\n<style type=\"text\/css\">\r\n\t#foogallery-gallery-5240 .fg-image {\r\n        width: 150px;\r\n    }\r\n<\/style>\r\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"foogallery foogallery-container foogallery-default foogallery-lightbox-foobox fg-gutter-10 fg-center fg-default fg-light fg-border-thin fg-shadow-outline fg-loading-default fg-loaded-fade-in fg-caption-hover fg-hover-fade fg-hover-zoom fg-ready\" id=\"foogallery-gallery-5240\" data-foogallery=\"{&quot;item&quot;:{&quot;showCaptionTitle&quot;:true,&quot;showCaptionDescription&quot;:true},&quot;lazy&quot;:true}\" >\r\n\t<div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/03\/DSC_3236.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"Designed in 1977 by Piet Blom, these unconventional buildings are called &lt;i&gt;Kubuswoningen&lt;\/i&gt; (or cube houses). The idea behind these houses was urban living; he wanted to optimize space and make them look like trees in a forest, with the cube as the foliage and the pylon as the stump.\" data-attachment-id=\"5254\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"Designed in 1977 by Piet Blom, these unconventional buildings are called &lt;i&gt;Kubuswoningen&lt;\/i&gt; (or cube houses). The idea behind these houses was urban living; he wanted to optimize space and make them look like trees in a forest, with the cube as the foliage and the pylon as the stump.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2020\/03\/DSC_3236\/1603156916.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">Designed in 1977 by Piet Blom, these unconventional buildings are called <i>Kubuswoningen<\/i> (or cube houses). The idea behind these houses was urban living; he wanted to optimize space and make them look like trees in a forest, with the cube as the foliage and the pylon as the stump.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/03\/DSC_3245.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"The goal of this architecture was to build 55 such houses in order to give the outside viewer the impression that this complex is an urban forest. In the end, only 39 houses were built, with one of those houses serving as a museum for the curious souls.\" data-attachment-id=\"5255\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"The goal of this architecture was to build 55 such houses in order to give the outside viewer the impression that this complex is an urban forest. In the end, only 39 houses were built, with one of those houses serving as a museum for the curious souls.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2020\/03\/DSC_3245\/280706006.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">The goal of this architecture was to build 55 such houses in order to give the outside viewer the impression that this complex is an urban forest. In the end, only 39 houses were built, with one of those houses serving as a museum for the curious souls.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https: