svg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">The top of the cube even features a chill out space with almost a 360-degree view.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/03\/DSC_3256.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"The bedroom\" data-attachment-id=\"5261\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"The bedroom\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2020\/03\/DSC_3256\/4200053965.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">The bedroom<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/03\/DSC_3247.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"The kitchen\" data-attachment-id=\"5256\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"The kitchen\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2020\/03\/DSC_3247\/1736606770.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">The kitchen<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/03\/DSC_3251.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"The office\" data-attachment-id=\"5258\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"The office\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2020\/03\/DSC_3251\/4062423363.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">The office<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/03\/DSC_3266.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"Lovingly referred to as the air conditioning unit, this building was designed by Van den Broek and built in 1983. Today it houses Rotterdam&#039;s Central Library. Some compare it to the Centre de Pompidou in Paris.\" data-attachment-id=\"5242\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"Lovingly referred to as the air conditioning unit, this building was designed by Van den Broek and built in 1983. Today it houses Rotterdam&#039;s Central Library. Some compare it to the Centre de Pompidou in Paris.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2020\/03\/DSC_3266\/125967617.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">Lovingly referred to as the air conditioning unit, this building was designed by Van den Broek and built in 1983. Today it houses Rotterdam's Central Library. Some compare it to the Centre de Pompidou in Paris.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/03\/DSC_3261.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"The Markthal faces Rotterdam&#039;s Central Library. This horseshoe-shaped building features a covered market hall on the ground floor with luxury housing in the actual structure.\" data-attachment-id=\"5262\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"The Markthal faces Rotterdam&#039;s Central Library. This horseshoe-shaped building features a covered market hall on the ground floor with luxury housing in the actual structure.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2020\/03\/DSC_3261\/4228067720.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">The Markthal faces Rotterdam's Central Library. This horseshoe-shaped building features a covered market hall on the ground floor with luxury housing in the actual structure.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/03\/DSC_3263.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"The inside of the horseshoe is painted by Arno Coenen and Iris Roskam. Because of the extensive painting job, some compare this building to the Sistine Chapel.\" data-attachment-id=\"5263\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"The inside of the horseshoe is painted by Arno Coenen and Iris Roskam. Because of the extensive painting job, some compare this building to the Sistine Chapel.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2020\/03\/DSC_3263\/469589181.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">The inside of the horseshoe is painted by Arno Coenen and Iris Roskam. Because of the extensive painting job, some compare this building to the Sistine Chapel.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/03\/DSC_3265.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"The statue located in the &lt;i&gt;Grotekerkplein&lt;\/i&gt; (or big church square) is of the most famous Rotterdamer: Desiderius Erasmus. Born in c. 1466, Erasmus imagined a better Europe without borders. This is one of the reasons why the study abroad semesters in Europe are referred to as Erasmus semesters and why so many study abroad programs and scholarships are named after this great thinker. Erasmus is quoted with having said: &quot; The whole world is your fatherland.&quot;\n&lt;p&gt;Erected in 1622, this statue has had an interesting history. Before building this statue in bronze, many other attempts were made to create an Erasmus statue but the statue was either destroyed or it was never finished. This one, designed by Hendrick de Keyser, was finished and stands to this day in the square. During the Second World War, it was even buried in the Boymans&#039; Museum to avoid its destruction by the German army. It is said that the people who hid the statue forgot about it for 14 years, at which point it was dug back out and placed on its pedestal in the square.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Given that Erasmus believed that churches should not dictate what you do, it is slightly ironic that his statue is placed in front of the only church that survived the bombings during the Second World War.&lt;\/p&gt;\" data-attachment-id=\"5241\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"The statue located in the &lt;i&gt;Grotekerkplein&lt;\/i&gt; (or big church square) is of the most famous Rotterdamer: Desiderius Erasmus. Born in c. 1466, Erasmus imagined a better Europe without borders. This is one of the reasons why the study abroad semesters in Europe are referred to as Erasmus semesters and why so many study abroad programs and scholarships are named after this great thinker. Erasmus is quoted with having said: &quot; The whole world is your fatherland.&quot;\n&lt;p&gt;Erected in 1622, this statue has had an interesting history. Before building this statue in bronze, many other attempts were made to create an Erasmus statue but the statue was either destroyed or it was never finished. This one, designed by Hendrick de Keyser, was finished and stands to this day in the square. During the Second World War, it was even buried in the Boymans&#039; Museum to avoid its destruction by the German army. It is said that the people who hid the statue forgot about it for 14 years, at which point it was dug back out and placed on its pedestal in the square.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Given that Erasmus believed that churches should not dictate what you do, it is slightly ironic that his statue is placed in front of the only church that survived the bombings during the Second World War.&lt;\/p&gt;\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2020\/03\/DSC_3265\/3155272315.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">The statue located in the <i>Grotekerkplein<\/i> (or big church square) is of the most famous Rotterdamer: Desiderius Erasmus. Born in c. 1466, Erasmus imagined a better Europe without borders. This is one of the reasons why the study abroad semesters in Europe are referred to as Erasmus semesters and why so many study abroad programs and scholarships are named after this great thinker. Erasmus is quoted with having said: \" The whole world is your fatherland.\"\n<p>Erected in 1622, this statue has had an interesting history. Before building this statue in bronze, many other attempts were made to create an Erasmus statue but the statue was either destroyed or it was never finished. This one, designed by Hendrick de Keyser, was finished and stands to this day in the square. During the Second World War, it was even buried in the Boymans' Museum to avoid its destruction by the German army. It is said that the people who hid the statue forgot about it for 14 years, at which point it was dug back out and placed on its pedestal in the square.<\/p>\n<p>Given that Erasmus believed that churches should not dictate what you do, it is slightly ironic that his statue is placed in front of the only church that survived the bombings during the Second World War.<\/p><\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/03\/DSC_3267.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"Not too far from the bronze statue is located yet another homage to the great Erasmus. This one is located on Eramus&#039; birthplace and features all of the thinker&#039;s most important quotes on Delft blue tiles.\" data-attachment-id=\"5243\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"Not too far from the bronze statue is located yet another homage to the great Erasmus. This one is located on Eramus&#039; birthplace and features all of the thinker&#039;s most important quotes on Delft blue tiles.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2020\/03\/DSC_3267\/1861449687.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">Not too far from the bronze statue is located yet another homage to the great Erasmus. This one is located on Eramus' birthplace and features all of the thinker's most important quotes on Delft blue tiles.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/03\/DSC_3268.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"If you search &quot;Rotterdam Second World War&quot; online, you will get multiple views of the same reality: Rotterdam flattened by German bombs. In all of those pictures, only a handful of buildings remain standing: this church being one of them. Built between 1449 and 1525, the &lt;i&gt;Laurenskerk&lt;\/i&gt;, or Church of St. Lawrence, is one of the few surviving Gothic buildings in the city. While it escaped most of the damage, there were still calls to demolish it and start over. Thanks to Queen Wilhelmina of the Netherlands, the church was preserved. Today, the church hold Friday evening disco parties for singles over 40.\" data-attachment-id=\"5244\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"If you search &quot;Rotterdam Second World War&quot; online, you will get multiple views of the same reality: Rotterdam flattened by German bombs. In all of those pictures, only a handful of buildings remain standing: this church being one of them. Built between 1449 and 1525, the &lt;i&gt;Laurenskerk&lt;\/i&gt;, or Church of St. Lawrence, is one of the few surviving Gothic buildings in the city. While it escaped most of the damage, there were still calls to demolish it and start over. Thanks to Queen Wilhelmina of the Netherlands, the church was preserved. Today, the church hold Friday evening disco parties for singles over 40.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2020\/03\/DSC_3268\/2016509441.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">If you search \"Rotterdam Second World War\" online, you will get multiple views of the same reality: Rotterdam flattened by German bombs. In all of those pictures, only a handful of buildings remain standing: this church being one of them. Built between 1449 and 1525, the <i>Laurenskerk<\/i>, or Church of St. Lawrence, is one of the few surviving Gothic buildings in the city. While it escaped most of the damage, there were still calls to demolish it and start over. Thanks to Queen Wilhelmina of the Netherlands, the church was preserved. Today, the church hold Friday evening disco parties for singles over 40.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/03\/DSC_3275.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"Rotterdam&#039;s City Hall is another of the buildings to have survived the 1940 bombing. The building features three flags: that of the EU, the Netherlands and Rotterdam (from left to right).\n&lt;p&gt;If you look further up, you will see a statue of a golden woman. It is said to be the golden whore who reminds everyone that sex always comes before politics.\" data-attachment-id=\"5248\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"Rotterdam&#039;s City Hall is another of the buildings to have survived the 1940 bombing. The building features three flags: that of the EU, the Netherlands and Rotterdam (from left to right).\n&lt;p&gt;If you look further up, you will see a statue of a golden woman. It is said to be the golden whore who reminds everyone that sex always comes before politics.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2020\/03\/DSC_3275\/540909047.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">Rotterdam's City Hall is another of the buildings to have survived the 1940 bombing. The building features three flags: that of the EU, the Netherlands and Rotterdam (from left to right).\n<p>If you look further up, you will see a statue of a golden woman. It is said to be the golden whore who reminds everyone that sex always comes before politics.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/03\/DSC_3270.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"In the rose garden within City Hall, there are two statues that remind visitors of the origins of the city. The statue on the left is of Neptune...\" data-attachment-id=\"5269\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"In the rose garden within City Hall, there are two statues that remind visitors of the origins of the city. The statue on the left is of Neptune...\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2020\/03\/DSC_3270\/1011014731.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">In the rose garden within City Hall, there are two statues that remind visitors of the origins of the city. The statue on the left is of Neptune...<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/03\/DSC_3271.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"while the statue on the right is of Mercury. The city of Rotterdam first began as a fishermen&#039;s village in c. 1270. Thus, Neptune represents the water while Mercury represents the trade of this early settlement.\" data-attachment-id=\"5245\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"while the statue on the right is of Mercury. The city of Rotterdam first began as a fishermen&#039;s village in c. 1270. Thus, Neptune represents the water while Mercury represents the trade of this early settlement.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2020\/03\/DSC_3271\/3588102945.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">while the statue on the right is of Mercury. The city of Rotterdam first began as a fishermen's village in c. 1270. Thus, Neptune represents the water while Mercury represents the trade of this early settlement.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/03\/DSC_3273.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"This statue has been in Rotterdam&#039;s city hall almost since its opening in 1920. It was a gift from Amsterdam in 1921 to celebrate its opening. The sculpture represents all the human struggles throughout time.\n&lt;p&gt;To get a more detailed description of all of the pieces of art and architecture in and on City Hall, feel free to &lt;a href=&quot;https:\/\/www.rotterdam.nl\/loket\/documentenkcc\/rotterdamCityhallGidsApril2016.pdf&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;explore this pamphlet&lt;\/u&gt;&lt;\/a&gt;.&lt;\/p&gt;\" data-attachment-id=\"5246\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"This statue has been in Rotterdam&#039;s city hall almost since its opening in 1920. It was a gift from Amsterdam in 1921 to celebrate its opening. The sculpture represents all the human struggles throughout time.\n&lt;p&gt;To get a more detailed description of all of the pieces of art and architecture in and on City Hall, feel free to &lt;a href=&quot;https:\/\/www.rotterdam.nl\/loket\/documentenkcc\/rotterdamCityhallGidsApril2016.pdf&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;explore this pamphlet&lt;\/u&gt;&lt;\/a&gt;.&lt;\/p&gt;\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2020\/03\/DSC_3273\/2733089989.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">This statue has been in Rotterdam's city hall almost since its opening in 1920. It was a gift from Amsterdam in 1921 to celebrate its opening. The sculpture represents all the human struggles throughout time.\n<p>To get a more detailed description of all of the pieces of art and architecture in and on City Hall, feel free to <a href=\"https:\/\