llen Germany. Gifted to City Hall by Queen Wilhelmina after the Second World War, the sculpture was created by J.H. Hans and weighs about 6 ton. The sculpture weighs so much that the floor of the town hall had to be reinforced with a pillar to support the weight.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/03\/DSC_3277.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"In contrast to Goliath, in front of City Hall stands a dark, unpolished sculpture depicting the pain caused by the tearing apart of families due to the war effort of the 1940s.\" data-attachment-id=\"5249\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"In contrast to Goliath, in front of City Hall stands a dark, unpolished sculpture depicting the pain caused by the tearing apart of families due to the war effort of the 1940s.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2020\/03\/DSC_3277\/3351507138.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">In contrast to Goliath, in front of City Hall stands a dark, unpolished sculpture depicting the pain caused by the tearing apart of families due to the war effort of the 1940s.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/03\/DSC_3278.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"&lt